(   [Problem Statement]: Trace the historical evolution of Design Thinking from Herbert Simon's 'Sciences of the Artificial' to Horst Rittel's 'Wicked Problems' and Stanford d.school.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Herbert Simon and Rational Design Theory \(1960s\):) Tj
T*
(   - In 'The Sciences of the Artificial' \(1969\), Nobel laureate Herbert A. Simon established) Tj
T*
(   design as a formal academic discipline distinct from natural sciences. While natural sciences) Tj
T*
(   explain existing reality, design conceives artifacts that transform existing conditions into) Tj
T*
(   preferred states. Simon introduced concepts of 'bounded rationality' and 'satisficing'.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Horst Rittel and Wicked Problems \(1970s\):) Tj
T*
(   - Horst Rittel and Melvin Webber \(1973\) rejected Simon's purely linear systems engineering) Tj
T*
(   models for complex social challenges, coining the term 'Wicked Problems'. Wicked problems have) Tj
T*
(   no definitive formulation, no ultimate stopping rule, solutions that are good/bad rather than) Tj
T*
(   true/false, and unique contextual constraints that cannot be solved by standard waterfall) Tj
T*
(   algorithms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Stanford University, Rolf Faste, and David Kelley \(1980s-2000s\):) Tj
T*
(   - Rolf Faste at Stanford integrated human-centred ambidextrous thinking \(combining analytical) Tj
T*
(   engineering with intuitive art\) into engineering curricula.) Tj
T*
(   - David Kelley, Bill Moggridge, and Mike Nuttall founded IDEO in 1991, institutionalizing) Tj
T*
(   design thinking in Silicon Valley product design.) Tj
T*
(   - In 2004, Kelley founded the Hasso Plattner Institute of Design at Stanford \(d.school\),) Tj
T*
(   codifying the five-stage methodology \(Empathize, Define, Ideate, Prototype, Test\) that) Tj
T*
(   democratized design methodology globally.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the five iterative stages of the Stanford d.school Design Thinking Framework. Explain why the process is fundamentally non-linear with an engineering feedback loop diagram.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Deconstruction of the Five Stages:) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 1: Empathize - Immersive field observation, shadowing, and contextual inquiry to) Tj
T*
(   uncover explicit and unarticulated emotional and cognitive user needs.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 2: Define - Synthesizing research data into a focused, human-centred Point-of-View) Tj
T*
(   \(POV\) statement and actionable 'How Might We' \(HMW\) design challenges.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 3: Ideate - Divergent idea generation deferring judgment \(Brainstorming, SCAMPER, Worst) Tj
T*
(   Idea\), followed by convergent prioritization matrices.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 4: Prototype - Building low-cost, quick, tangible representations \(paper UI sketches,) Tj
T*
(   wireframes, Wizard of Oz mockups\) to externalize ideas.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 5: Test - Placing artifacts before genuine target users in realistic task environments) Tj
T*
ET

