(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze IDEO's Three Lenses of Innovation: Desirability, Feasibility, and Viability. Illustrate with a comprehensive comparative case study of a balanced product versus an imbalanced product.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Architecture of the Three Lenses:) Tj
T*
(   - Desirability \(People\): Does this solution address a genuine human pain point? Does it fit) Tj
T*
(   into user mental models, emotional desires, and daily workflows?) Tj
T*
(   - Feasibility \(Technology\): Can this solution be engineered using available or near-term) Tj
T*
(   hardware, software, materials, and infrastructure within physical constraints?) Tj
T*
(   - Viability \(Business\): Does this solution fit a sustainable, scalable business model with) Tj
T*
(   viable unit economics, customer acquisition costs, and lifetime value?) Tj
T*
(   - The Innovation Sweet Spot lies exclusively at the intersection of all three lenses.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Balanced Case Study: Apple iPhone \(2007\):) Tj
T*
(   - Desirability: Seamless multi-touch glass interface, full web browser, and iPod music player) Tj
T*
(   in one pocketable device.) Tj
T*
(   - Feasibility: Capacitive touchscreen sensors, energy-efficient ARM processors, and custom OS X) Tj
T*
(   Unix kernel executed at massive scale.) Tj
T*
(   - Viability: Revolutionary revenue-sharing carrier partnerships \(AT&T\) followed by a 30%) Tj
T*
(   commission App Store ecosystem.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Imbalanced Case Study: Segway Personal Transporter \(2001\):) Tj
T*
(   - High Feasibility: Remarkable gyroscopic self-balancing dynamic stabilization technology.) Tj
T*
(   - Catastrophic Desirability & Viability Deficits: Priced at $5,000 \(beyond consumer reach\),) Tj
T*
(   weighed 100 lbs \(impractical to transport\), lacked sidewalk or road regulatory infrastructure,) Tj
T*
(   and imposed social embarrassment on riders. Resulted in commercial disaster.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 8:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Critically evaluate Doug Dietz's 'Adventure Series' pediatric MRI redesign at GE Healthcare. How did empathetic observation transform clinical outcomes without modifying the core physical machine?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Context and Problem Identification:) Tj
T*
(   - Doug Dietz, a veteran industrial designer at GE Healthcare, designed an ultra-sophisticated,) Tj
T*
(   multi-million-dollar MRI scanner.) Tj
T*
(   - Upon visiting a pediatric imaging clinic, he discovered the terrifying reality: to young) Tj
T*
(   children, the massive, humming machine, flickering warning lights, and cold clinical room felt) Tj
T*
(   like a torture dungeon.) Tj
T*
