(   [Problem Statement]: Contrast 'Divergent Thinking' and 'Convergent Thinking'. Explain how the Double Diamond framework balances both thinking modes across the product innovation lifecycle.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Cognitive Characteristics of Divergent vs. Convergent Thinking:) Tj
T*
(   - Divergent Thinking: Generative, expansive, exploratory, and non-judgmental. It seeks to) Tj
T*
(   maximize the quantity and variety of possibilities from a single starting point, encouraging) Tj
T*
(   wild ideas and cross-disciplinary analogies.) Tj
T*
(   - Convergent Thinking: Analytical, critical, selective, and deductive. It evaluates) Tj
T*
(   possibilities against objective criteria \(feasibility, budget, physical laws\) to converge on) Tj
T*
(   the single optimal decision.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Structure of the Double Diamond Model \(Design Council, 2004\):) Tj
T*
(   - Diamond 1 \(Problem Space\):) Tj
T*
(   * Phase 1: Discover \(Diverge\) - Broad user research, open-ended ethnographic immersion,) Tj
T*
(   shadowing, and contextual inquiry.) Tj
T*
(   * Phase 2: Define \(Converge\) - Synthesizing data, clustering pain points, eliminating noise,) Tj
T*
(   and crystallizing the single core challenge in a Point-of-View statement.) Tj
T*
(   - Diamond 2 \(Solution Space\):) Tj
T*
(   * Phase 3: Develop \(Diverge\) - Uninhibited ideation, paper prototyping, brainstorming,) Tj
T*
(   exploring radically different architectural concepts.) Tj
T*
(   * Phase 4: Deliver \(Converge\) - Rigorous usability testing, stress testing, engineering) Tj
T*
(   validation, and shipping the final minimum viable product.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Common Anti-Patterns:) Tj
T*
(   - Premature Convergence: Jumping into coding an obvious solution during Diamond 1 without) Tj
T*
(   verifying if the core problem was correctly framed.) Tj
T*
(   - Endless Divergence: Analysis paralysis, generating infinite whiteboard sticky notes without) Tj
T*
(   ever converging into executable prototypes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 13:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Define 'Wicked Problems' as articulated by Horst Rittel. Why are modern cybersecurity and socio-technical software systems classified as wicked problems?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Horst Rittel's Ten Criteria of Wicked Problems \(1973\):) Tj
T*
(   - No definitive formulation: Defining the problem is the problem.) Tj
T*
(   - No stopping rule: The problem cannot be marked 'done'; work stops due to resource depletion.) Tj
T*
(   - Solutions are not true-or-false, but good-or-bad or satisficing.) Tj
T*
(   - No immediate or ultimate test of a solution: Consequences reverberate indefinitely.) Tj
T*
(   - Every solution is a 'one-shot operation' because every intervention alters the system) Tj
T*
(   irreversibly.) Tj
T*
(   - No enumerable list of potential solutions.) Tj
T*
(   - Every wicked problem is essentially unique and symptomatic of another problem.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Socio-Technical Systems & Cybersecurity as Wicked Problems:) Tj
T*
(   - Dynamic Adversarial Evolution: In enterprise cybersecurity, the threat landscape shifts) Tj
T*
(   continuously. Defending against ransomware alters attacker economics, prompting supply-chain) Tj
T*
(   attacks. There is no static mathematical proof of total security.) Tj
T*
(   - Conflicting Stakeholder Values: Security requirements \(zero-trust authentication, biometric) Tj
T*
(   scans, encrypted enclaves\) directly conflict with user convenience, employee productivity, and) Tj
T*
ET

