(   [Problem Statement]: Contrast the 'Design-Driven Innovation' framework formulated by Roberto Verganti with traditional user-pull and technology-push innovation models.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Three Innovation Paradigms:) Tj
T*
(   - Market Pull \(User-Centred\): Innovation begins by listening to existing user requests and) Tj
T*
(   analyzing visible consumer needs. It typically results in incremental improvements because) Tj
T*
(   users cannot ask for things outside their mental framework.) Tj
T*
(   - Technology Push: Innovation driven by radical scientific breakthroughs and R&D lab) Tj
T*
(   discoveries seeking a market application \(e.g., the transistor, synthetic polymers\).) Tj
T*
(   - Design-Driven Innovation \(Verganti\): Innovation of Meaning. It proposes novel, unexpected) Tj
T*
(   interpretations of what a product means in society, changing the fundamental reason why people) Tj
T*
(   use the artifact.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Comparative Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Apple iPod: Technology push provided micro-hard drives; design-driven innovation transformed) Tj
T*
(   music listening from 'owning vinyl/CD albums' to 'having 1,000 songs in your pocket as an) Tj
T*
(   expression of personal identity'.) Tj
T*
(   - Swatch: Transformed the watch from an expensive, lifelong precision timekeeping instrument) Tj
T*
(   \(Swiss tradition\) into a cheap, colorful, disposable fashion accessory to be changed daily.) Tj
T*
(   - Nintendo Wii: Transformed video consoles from solitary graphical simulations for hardcore) Tj
T*
(   gamers into an active, social, physical party experience for the entire family.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Strategic Significance:) Tj
T*
(   - While user research ensures usability, design-driven meaning creation creates blue-ocean) Tj
T*
(   markets insulated from commoditization.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
