/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the role of 'Perceptual Blocks' in human-computer interaction \(HCI\). How do perceptual illusions and cognitive blindness impact the design of safety-critical avionics cockpit software?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Psychological Definition of Perceptual Blocks:) Tj
T*
(   - Perceptual blocks are cognitive impediments that prevent an observer from correctly detecting) Tj
T*
(   or interpreting sensory data in their environment.) Tj
T*
(   - Phenomena include 'Inattentional Blindness' \(failing to see an obvious stimulus because) Tj
T*
(   attention is focused elsewhere\) and 'Change Blindness' \(failing to notice substantial changes) Tj
T*
(   in a visual scene\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Impact on Avionics Cockpit Software:) Tj
T*
(   - Cognitive Tunneling: Under severe flight turbulence or emergency equipment failures, pilots) Tj
T*
(   experience intense sympathetic stress, narrowing attention onto a single malfunctioning gauge) Tj
T*
(   while missing primary attitude indicators.) Tj
T*
(   - Clutter & Mode Confusion: If electronic flight displays present hundreds of overlapping) Tj
T*
(   alphanumeric readouts, visual saliency degrades. Pilots cannot differentiate between autopilot) Tj
T*
(   modes \(e.g., Vertical Speed vs. Flight Path Angle\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Human-Centred Design Countermeasures:) Tj
T*
(   - Synthetic Vision Systems \(SVS\): Rendering clear 3D terrain cues that match the pilot's) Tj
T*
ET

