(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the 'Kano Model' of customer satisfaction. Categorize the features of a modern mobile banking smartphone application into Must-be, One-dimensional, and Attractive qualities.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Architecture of the Kano Model:) Tj
T*
(   - Developed by Professor Noriaki Kano \(1984\), the model maps the relationship between customer) Tj
T*
(   satisfaction and product functionality across distinct emotional categories:) Tj
T*
(   * Must-be \(Basic\): Expected threshold requirements. If missing, customers are furious; if) Tj
T*
(   present, satisfaction does not rise above neutral.) Tj
T*
(   * One-dimensional \(Performance\): Linear attributes. Better execution directly increases) Tj
T*
(   customer satisfaction \(e.g., faster speed, lower fees\).) Tj
T*
(   * Attractive \(Delighters\): Unexpected innovations that produce exponential delight when) Tj
T*
(   present, but cause zero dissatisfaction if absent.) Tj
T*
(   * Reverse / Indifferent: Features that users actively dislike or do not care about.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Application to Mobile Banking Application:) Tj
T*
(   - Must-be \(Threshold\): 256-bit SSL encryption, 100% balance accuracy, instant biometric login) Tj
T*
(   \(FaceID\), view transaction history, and 24/7 server uptime. Missing these triggers immediate) Tj
T*
(   account closure.) Tj
T*
(   - One-dimensional \(Performance\): Latency of inter-bank money transfers \(instant vs. 2 days\),) Tj
T*
(   search performance across multi-year PDF statements, and app startup speed.) Tj
T*
(   - Attractive \(Delighters\): AI-driven automated tax categorization, predictive overdraft alerts) Tj
T*
(   with zero penalty fees, instant virtual burner debit cards for safe online shopping, and) Tj
T*
(   one-tap automated micro-investing on spare change.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Dynamic Drift:) Tj
T*
(   - Mobile check deposit was a revolutionary Delighter in 2011; today, it has decayed into an) Tj
T*
(   absolute Must-be expectation across all banks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 25:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
