12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the 'Design Debt' phenomenon in modern agile software development. How does it differ from 'Technical Debt', and what is its cumulative impact on customer retention?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definitional Distinctions:) Tj
T*
(   - Technical Debt \(Ward Cunningham\): The cumulative cost of sub-optimal architectural shortcuts,) Tj
T*
(   missing unit tests, and deprecated code libraries taken to accelerate immediate feature) Tj
T*
(   delivery. It affects maintainability and code velocity.) Tj
T*
(   - Design Debt: The cumulative buildup of inconsistent UI components, fractured user flows,) Tj
T*
(   redundant menus, legacy interactions, and orphaned UX patterns that accumulate when features) Tj
T*
(   are added incrementally without holistic design governance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Root Causes in Agile Sprints:) Tj
T*
(   - Two-week sprint cadences prioritize shipping isolated functional user stories \('As a user, I) Tj
T*
(   want a button to export CSV'\). Over 50 sprints, five different engineering teams create five) Tj
T*
(   distinct modal dialogs, four different icon sets, and three conflicting navigation bars.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Cumulative Impact on Customer Experience & Retention:) Tj
T*
(   - Cognitive Friction: Users expend excessive mental energy re-learning basic interactions) Tj
T*
(   across different screens, increasing error rates and frustration.) Tj
T*
(   - Brand Erosion: The software feels unpolished, fragile, and amateurish, eroding user trust in) Tj
T*
(   the underlying reliability and security of the product.) Tj
T*
(   - Churn: Modern SaaS buyers have zero tolerance for clunky software; intuitive consumer-grade) Tj
T*
(   competitors \(e.g., Slack displacing HipChat, Notion displacing legacy wikis\) readily) Tj
T*
(   cannibalize enterprise accounts burdened with heavy design debt.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 29:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Evaluate the role of 'Empathy Mapping' in synthesizing qualitative user research. Detail the four traditional quadrants \(Says, Thinks, Does, Feels\) and explain how identifying contradictions yields breakthrough insights.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture of the Empathy Map:) Tj
T*
(   - Developed by Dave Gray, an Empathy Map is a visual collaborative synthesis tool that captures) Tj
T*
(   a comprehensive portrait of a user segment within a specific scenario, divided into four core) Tj
T*
(   quadrants:) Tj
T*
